# Golden example outputs are compared byte-for-byte against interpreter
# output (always \n), so nothing may be CRLF-converted on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The dirty fixtures selftest/bytes.ting reads are bytes, not text: a
# latin-1 log, a character cut in half, a NUL, CRLF, a BOM. Any
# conversion at all — including the eol=lf above — destroys what they
# are there to test, so git may not touch them.
selftest/fixtures/** -text
